IMPORT `ei6-schedule-rows`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Schedule I (subsection 12(2)): the table of weeks of benefits.
-- Written by piece ei6 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24; the rows below were generated by a script that reads the raw file
-- (src:3205-3245), so no figure is typed by hand. Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws
-- consolidation current to 2026-09-30; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- What the table decides: the maximum number of weeks of regular benefits (s 12(2), piece ei1) for a claimant, by the
-- number of hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period (the rows) and the regional rate of unemployment
-- that applies to the claimant (the columns). Which hours and which rate apply are decided by ss 7, 8 and 14 and by
-- reg 17 (pieces ei1, er1): here they are plain inputs.
--
-- Three readings, each in the fork register of NOTES.md:
--   * a blank cell is NOTHING: the table gives no number of weeks there (such a claimant does not reach the hours s 7
--     and s 7.1 require at that rate, but those sections are outside this piece, so the table does not say so);
--   * fewer than 420 hours has no row, so it is NOTHING;
--   * a count of hours between two rows (454.5) belongs to the lower row: hours are counted whole, and a row begins on
--     the hour its label gives.

§ `Schedule I - Table of Weeks of Benefits`

